Reason: SMS_EV_HIDE_PLAYER_MODEL (port_ext_hide_player_model) left FLUDD drawn when a BetterSunshineEngine mod answers isYoshiMaintainFluddModel (0x8024D68C, Super Mario Eclipse): the hook was only asked on the game's own branch of the test. It is now asked first, so FLUDD goes with the player's models in every build (a first-person camera, multiplayer's own character).

--- a/src/Player/MarioMain.cpp
+++ b/src/Player/MarioMain.cpp
@@ -213,19 +213,16 @@
 			// BetterSunshineEngine (isYoshiMaintainFluddModel, retail
 			// 0x8024D68C, with the word at 0x8024D690: cmpwi r3, 0): its
 			// result (it reads this from r31) replaces the FLUDD flag test.
-			if (SMS_MOD_SITE(0x8024D68C)
+			// an extension may draw the player its own way (port_ext.h): FLUDD
+			// goes with him, whatever a mod's isYoshiMaintainFluddModel says
+			if (!port_ext_hide_player_model(this)
+			    && (SMS_MOD_SITE(0x8024D68C)
 			        ? (SMS_MOD_GPR(31, this),
 			           ((bool (*)())SMS_MOD_SITE(0x8024D68C))())
-			        :
+			        : checkFlag(MARIO_FLAG_HAS_FLUDD)))
 #else
-			if (
+			if (checkFlag(MARIO_FLAG_HAS_FLUDD))
 #endif
-			    checkFlag(MARIO_FLAG_HAS_FLUDD)
-#ifdef TARGET_PC
-			    // an extension may draw the player its own way (port_ext.h)
-			    && !port_ext_hide_player_model(this)
-#endif
-			    )
 				MarioMainGetFludd(this)->perform(CUE_ENTRY, graphics);
 
 #ifdef TARGET_PC
